findings.description:
The design says retyping `inferredStatus` alone would leave `taskFileParser.ts`'s bare-string assignments "failing to compile". They would compile: `'complete'` is assignable to `NormalizedStatus`, because the retype only widens. Every consumer already accepts `NormalizedStatus`:
- `slice.ts:76`;
- `WorkflowNavigator.ts:655`;
- `types.ts:276` and `:321`.

All steps are independent, so the ordering constraint and the coupled step 1 can be dropped. The steps could also be one reviewable diff.
